    "submission": "submission-phase1-record.json",
    "summary": "Turn 51 found a second defect in the durability path and submitted its check.\n\nThe lead. startPhase1 installs the new instance under the owner's row, InstanceSpace[replica][instance], and then records metadata for InstanceSpace[r.Id][instance] — the recovering replica's own row. In the recovery-led phase 1 (the restart taken by prepare sub-cases 5 and 6) the leader is not the owner, so that slot belongs to a different instance or to nothing at all, and the recorder dereferences whatever it is given.\n\nObservation. With Durable true, an empty own row and startPhase1 called for another replica's instance, the local construction run reports panicked true with a nil pointer dereference, while the owner's record was installed (owner_record_written true). So the failure is in the recording call rather than in the instance setup, and the call that was supposed to persist the recovering instance's context wrote — or tried to write — a different row. The harness wraps only the call in recover() to observe the panic, and the handlers are unmodified.\n\nObligation and check (new claim C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row, implementation semantics, priority 1). The duty is that the metadata recorder must be given the record of the instance being written and must not dereference a record the replica does not hold. The check asserts panicked == false on the recording result, with the durability flag and the empty own row as prerequisite conditions, instance identity correlation and a new binding (BB10-phase1-record) on the phase-1 entry. The claim's scope is the recovery-led case with an empty own row; the slot-exists case — where the source implies another instance's metadata would be recorded — is an explicit unknown rather than a claim, and the shipped configuration's durable=false keeps the importance bounded.\n\nState. Audit spec version 11; the eight settled claims and their scopes are untouched, the executor-timeout protection (C8) was confirmed this cycle, the two paused candidates keep their resume conditions, and the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact remains the only visible administrative item. No requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
